            <ArticleTitle>Case report: haemorrhagic mesenteric cyst mimicking appendicitis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>137-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A five-year old girl who presented with an acute abdominal emergency was found to have a haemorrhagic mesenteric cyst intraoperatively. The clinical picture and the mode of management are presented and discussed. The possibility of a complicated mesenteric cyst should be considered in the differential diagnosis in patients with an acute abdomen.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
